## Encounter Analysis

Encounter count by class:
- Ambulatory: 3,225
- Wellness: 1,371
- Outpatient: 886
- Emergency: 216
- Urgent Care: 162
- Inpatient: 101

Findings:
- Ambulatory encounters were the most common encounter type.
- Wellness and outpatient visits were also common.
- Emergency and inpatient encounters represented a small portion of total encounters.

### Encounter Cost Analysis

Average claim cost by encounter class:

- Inpatient: $22,822.83
- SNF: $18,116.74
- Hospice: $9,552.20
- Emergency: $3,729.75
- Ambulatory: $3,120.58

Findings:
- Inpatient encounters had the highest average claim cost.
- Ambulatory encounters were the most common encounter type but were not the most expensive.
- High-cost encounter classes (inpatient, SNF, hospice) represented relatively few encounters.
- Ambulatory encounters were the most common encounter type (3,225 encounters).
- Inpatient encounters had the highest average claim cost ($22,822.83).
- Ambulatory encounters generated the highest total claim cost (~$10.1 million).
- Although inpatient encounters were significantly more expensive per encounter, ambulatory encounters drove overall spending due to high utilization.

### Encounter Utilization by Age Group

Encounters per patient:

- Under 18: 22.28
- 18-34: 35.47
- 35-49: 43.41
- 50-64: 50.46
- 65+: 107.88

Findings:

- Encounter utilization increased with age.
- Patients aged 65+ averaged 107.88 encounters per patient.
- The 65+ age group generated more than twice as many encounters per patient as the 50-64 age group.
- Age-related increases in encounter utilization mirrored age-related increases in claim utilization.